      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Dr Wood, an expert in the intersection of political and religious ideas in the late antique Middle East, chaired a session on Change and Renewal in Non-Muslim Communal Outlooks in the Classical Islamic Period on Thursday 9th July. Concentrating on aspects of adaptation, adjustment, and modification by "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "non-Muslim communities",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "attrs": {
                    "href": "https://imc.leeds.ac.uk/dbsql02/AQueryServlet?%2aid=30&%2aformId=30&%2acontext=IMC&conference=2015&sessionId=5618&chosenPaperId=&%2aservletURI=https://imc.leeds.ac.uk/dbsql02/AQueryServlet",
                    "target": "_self",
                    "linktype": "url",
                    "uuid": null,
                    "anchor": null,
                    "custom": {}
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " in the context of life under Muslim rule, speakers looked at social and administrative change. More information about the session is available here."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
